    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

    Targets: FreeBASIC fb dialect; shared Windows/Linux x64 and Android editor builds.

    Module API: Implements ui_icons.bi; declarations there define the shared interface.

    Purpose:

        Provide a deterministic grayscale bitmap atlas for compact editor
        icons which must look the same on Windows and Linux.

    Responsibilities:

        - retain checked 24 x 24 hexadecimal coverage masks
        - return bounded mask rows without exposing atlas storage
        - convert four-bit coverage into backend-ready eight-bit alpha

    This file intentionally does NOT contain:

        - RGB subpixel rendering, whose channel order is display-dependent
        - graphics-backend calls or image-file loading
        - widget layout, theme selection, or input handling
'/

#lang "fb"

#include once "ui_icons.bi"

/'
    Coverage atlas

    Each hexadecimal digit stores one grayscale coverage sample. The masks
    were supersampled at eight positions per axis, then hand-aligned to the
    24-pixel control grid. This gives diagonal and curved edges intermediate
    alpha without depending on a platform font rasterizer or RGB stripe order.
'/
